# The old React /blog page is gone. Its posts were removed as unpublishable
# (fabricated bylines, unsourced statistics). Send readers and crawlers to the
# real blog. 301 = permanent, so search engines transfer any accrued signal.
/blog        https://blog.onealgorithm.com/    301
/blog/*      https://blog.onealgorithm.com/    301

# Anything that matches no file is genuinely missing, so say so.
#
# Cloudflare Pages was serving 404.html for unknown paths but with a 200 status,
# which is a soft 404: /wp-login.php, /.env and every mistyped link looked like a
# valid page to a crawler. Bing had crawled thousands of URLs against a sitemap
# of 28. Setting not_found_handling on the project is ignored on classic Pages
# projects, so the status has to come from here.
#
# MUST STAY LAST. Pages serves a matching static asset before consulting this
# file, and all 28 real routes are prerendered as static files by
# scripts/prerender.mjs, so nothing legitimate reaches this rule.
/*           /404.html                         404
